      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HOUSE PARTY (2) worked to find the lead and kept kicking only to find one better last start at Swan Hill, making it two minor placings on the bounce. Both of those were from wider barriers so she should enjoy a nice run from this favourable starting position. Gets her chance to break through. HAPPILY (3) drew on the back row and made up plenty of ground to get the prize by a head at her latest appearance at Ballarat. Should have no excuses from this advantageous draw. Could deliver again. RIVER STORM (4) will find this easier than when he tackled some good three-year-olds at Melton two weeks ago. Scored at Cranbourne prior and won the only time he attempted this distance. SECRET SERVICE AGENT NZ (7) draws wide but has claims off a win two back at Melton.",
